htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_FontSet                  htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_FontSet

   NAME
    HTMLTTF_FontSet -- (STRPTR) font family (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    "Vera"   Vera.ttf VeraBd.ttf VeraIt.ttf VeraBI.ttf VeraMono.ttf ...
    "DejaVu" DejaVuSans.ttf DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf ... DejaVuSansMono.ttf ...
    "Noto"   NotoSans-Regular.ttf NotoSans-Bold.ttf ... NotoSansMono-Regular.ttf
    Default: the first family found in this order. Missing bold or italic
    variants are synthesized.
htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_FontSetName          htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_FontSetName

   NAME
    HTMLTTF_FontSetName -- (STRPTR) the family in use (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    NULL if no TrueType font was found; then no text can be drawn.
htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_GetClass                htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_GetClass

   NAME
    HTMLTTF_GetClass -- get a pointer to the htmlttf.gadget class (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
    class = HTMLTTF_GetClass();
    D0

    Class *HTMLTTF_GetClass(VOID);

   FUNCTION
    Returns the class pointer for NewObject(). The class is public as well,
    so after OpenLibrary() NewObject(NULL, "htmlttf.gadget", ...) works too.

   RESULT
    class - pointer to the class, never NULL while the library is open.
htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_Size                        htmlttf.gadget/HTMLTTF_Size

   NAME
    HTMLTTF_Size -- (LONG) pixel size of the body text (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    Default: derived from the default public screen's font (13 -> 12).
    HTML sizes 1..7 are 8/10/12/14/18/24/36 twelfths of it.
